# Caddyfile for naviamp-sidecar + Navidrome
#
# Caddy sits in front of both containers and routes by URL path:
#   /naviamp/*  →  naviamp-sidecar:8090
#   everything  →  navidrome:4533
#
# This means clients only need one address. The Naviamp app probes
# <serverUrl>/naviamp/capabilities on startup — with Caddy in front,
# that probe reaches the sidecar automatically with no extra configuration
# on the client side.
#
# Caddy evaluates matchers top-to-bottom; the first match wins.
# The two reverse_proxy lines below are all that's needed — no regex.
#
# ── Local / no domain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use this block if you're running on a local network without a domain name.
# Caddy serves plain HTTP on port 80.

:80 {
    reverse_proxy /naviamp/* naviamp-sidecar:8090
    reverse_proxy * navidrome:4533
}

# ── Public domain with automatic HTTPS ───────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment this block (and remove the :80 block above) if you have a domain
# name pointing at this server. Caddy obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt TLS
# certificate automatically — no certbot, no manual renewal.
#
# Replace "music.example.com" with your actual domain.
#
# music.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy /naviamp/* naviamp-sidecar:8090
#     reverse_proxy * navidrome:4533
# }
